  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY NIGHT THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 109 PM MDT Thu Aug 27 2026\n\nThe upper ridge will continue slowly shifting east this weekend, \nwith strengthening southwest flow aloft. Temperatures will continue \nto warm, with the far eastern plains hitting the 100-degree mark in \nsome places. Meanwhile, monsoon moisture will return the our \nmountains, allowing for increased coverage of afternoon \nshowers/thunderstorms over the Continental Divide, with isolated to \nscattered storms over our eastern mountains. Mid-level steering flow \nwill likely push a few storms onto the I-25 corridor as well, but \nlingering dry air and downsloping winds near the surface will keep \nmost activity away from the eastern plains.\n\nLate Sunday into early Monday, and upper wave will swing past to our \nnorth, sending a cold front south across the eastern plains. \nActivity over the plains remains limited, and temperatures behind \nthe front only cool a few degrees in the latest guidance. The \nmountains will continue to see daily showers and storms. Looking \nfurther into next week, long-range models suggest a slightly drier \npattern returning as the monsoon plume shifts a bit further to our \nwest.",
